# Line endings are normalised on the way into the index and back out on
# checkout. Everyone here works on Windows and `.prettierrc.json` sets
# `endOfLine: "lf"`, so without this the repository would fill with CRLF.
#
# WHAT THIS DOES NOT DO, because it has already been proposed twice as a fix
# for a problem it cannot solve: it does not stop `pnpm format:check` failing
# on a file an editor has just written with CRLF. These rules act on the
# index/worktree boundary — commit and checkout. Prettier reads the working
# tree directly, where a freshly written CRLF file sits unconverted until it
# has been committed and checked out again. A newly saved file is exactly the
# case that never reaches this filter.
#
# The symptom is distinctive: prettier reports every line in the file as
# changed while the content is byte-identical. If you see that, run
# `pnpm format` — do not go looking for a semantic difference, and do not add
# a `.gitattributes` rule, which is already here and already did its job.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.pdf binary
*.docx binary
*.xlsx binary

pnpm-lock.yaml -diff linguist-generated
packages/db/drizzle/meta/** -diff linguist-generated
